  "result": "The per-person list is decided by `visibleNav()` in `src/config/nav.ts`. It walks `SIDEBAR_NAV` and `SETTINGS_NAV` and drops each item that fails either check:\n\n- **Role:** items with an `action` are checked with `can()` from `src/lib/permissions.ts`, which maps each action to a minimum role in `ROLE_MATRIX`. That is why admins and viewers see different entries.\n- **Plan:** items with a `flag` are checked against the flag snapshot, falling back to `isEnabled()` with `plan: \"free\"` when the snapshot lacks the key. That is why some entries are missing for cheaper plans.\n\n`src/components/domain/nav/app-sidebar.tsx` only calls `visibleNav()` and renders the result. It does not decide which entries appear. The Projects section has its own `project:read` gate in that component, but it is not part of the nav tree.\n\nI did not open `src/lib/feature-flags.ts` to confirm how the snapshot is built for each plan, so that part rests on the fallback code in `nav.ts`.\n\nANSWER: src/config/nav.ts",
